      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree. 50mb is a hard target to hit unless you have a super small world. And this is me after super optimizing every nook and cranny, crunching every tiny image, stripping shaders, and so on. 100mb would be sufficient for a green world. Orange for 150. Etc. I completely agree with the size ratings",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
